There seems to be some confusion between the _practice_ of a cult and the
_content_ of a cult. I've heard no one on this list attempt to argue the
validity of the teachings of Koresh and the Branch Davidians (nor, for that
matter, have I ever heard of anyone on this list arguing for the truth of
the Bible, at least not in the 8 months I've been reading the list).

The issue on the BD/Waco assault was never the _content_ of their
teachings. I suspect very few of us care one way or another what Koresh
believes, what Seventh Day Adventists believe, etc. Thus, our "support" for
religious freedom (a subset of the larger freedom to be left alone) says
nothing about our support for the belief systems of Branch Davidian, of
Odin worshippers, of Jews, or of any other cult.

A BATF assault on a bunch of tree worshippers in Humboldt County would be
just as strongly opposed by most of us, I'm sure. And if flying yogis were
grounded, I'd be supporting them, too.

